body:
### Description

I configured lsp/bashls.lua as below:
```lua
return {
    filetypes = {'zsh'},
    settings = {a = 5}
}
```

Then did :checkhealth vim.lsp:
```yaml
- bashls (id: 2)
  - Version: ? (no serverInfo.version response)
  - Root directory: ~/.dotfiles
  - Command: { "bash-language-server", "start" }
  - Settings: {
      a = 5,
      bashIde = {
        globPattern = "*@(.sh|.inc|.bash|.command)"
      }
    }
  - Attached buffers: 18
```
It works with other LSPs, but for bashls, settings is successfully applied while filetypes is completely ignored.

